10
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:20,562
<i>She ended up choosing Ari.</i>

11
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:21,896
MARIRIN (25)
BAR WORKER

12
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:24,190
Okay.

13
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:26,693
- Have fun.
- We'll be back.

14
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,571
I'll help you clear up these plates.

15
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:31,322
- Thanks.
- Yeah, this was good.

16
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:36,870
- We haven't really talked.
- Yeah.

17
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:40,373
The last time was when me and Taisei
were talking with you in the living room.

18
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:41,708
That's about it.

19
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:45,378
It's good to look each other in the eyes.
We can understand one another.

20
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:47,297
I agree.

21
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:51,092
Well, yeah, a lot's happened.

22
00:00:52,385 --> 00:00:54,137
So I wanted to hear how you felt.

23
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:57,891
Honestly, I'm starting to hate myself
for being so cautious.

24
00:00:57,974 --> 00:00:58,808
Yeah.

25
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,603
- I've been cheated on before…
- Mmm-hmm.

26
00:01:01,686 --> 00:01:03,104
…so I tend to be cautious.

27
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:04,939
So when people are like,

28
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,233
"Just make up your mind
and choose already,"

29
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:10,236
honestly, that's been pretty hard
on me lately.

30
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:12,781
Mmm, I see.

31
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:16,034
I mean, what happened
with the omelet rice earlier…

32
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:19,871
was because Maririn said
she was interested in you.

33
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:22,540
She told us she wanted to write on yours.

34
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:26,002
And Ha-chan said
she wanted to write on Tai-chan's.

35
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:27,837
I wasn't sure of anything anymore.

36
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:30,548
So I told them, like, "Sure, go ahead."

37
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:32,175
Mmm.

38
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:34,677
If I gave it to one of you
when I haven't made up my mind,

39
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:36,721
that would be another mixed signal.

40
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:40,266
You know how people start liking someone
when they get jealous?

41
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,184
Oh.

42
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:43,603
I thought I could understand
my feelings better

43
00:01:43,686 --> 00:01:45,772
if I made things more exciting,

44
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:48,399
so I thought yesterday
was both good and bad.

45
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,360
- Right.
- You were holding hands with her.

46
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:51,945
Uh, yeah.

47
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:55,573
<i>Well, my feelings</i>
<i>were kind of all over the place that day.</i>

48
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:58,118
<i>At one moment, I was lost for words,</i>

49
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:02,205
and she said something like,
"I can accept everything about you, Ari."

50
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:03,206
I said, "Thanks."

51
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:04,707
She was like, "You can hold my hands."

52
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:07,085
"Take your time and share with me
how you're feeling."

53
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,545
Can she really understand you, though?

54
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:11,756
Maybe she's just saying that.

55
00:02:21,724 --> 00:02:23,476
- Are you having fun?
- No.

56
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,477
You're not?

57
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:26,104
- Do I look like I'm having fun?
- Yeah.

58
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:27,021
- Really?
- Are you bored?

59
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,439
No, I'm having fun.

60
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:30,942
- I've just been stressing over things.
- These past few days?

61
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:34,487
I've been stressing over things
so much that I'm almost hating myself.

62
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,114
Really.

63
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:38,283
I was in such a bad place.

64
00:02:38,366 --> 00:02:39,784
Seriously.

65
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:42,370
I don't know if I can fall in love.

66
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:46,499
Talking to Maririn
made me realize some things.

67
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:49,085
Like, I can tell
she really came here to fall in love.

68
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:50,003
Mmm.

69
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:52,839
And I can see her being someone
who'd take time to support me.

70
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:58,011
We don't have
that many days left, you know?

71
00:02:58,094 --> 00:03:01,097
Right. I don't want it to end
with, "Time's up."

72
00:03:01,181 --> 00:03:04,893
So, for example, if you're still
equally interested in both me and Taisei,

73
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:07,645
or if you kind of like him more,

74
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:10,523
then I'd want to spend my time
with Maririn.

75
00:03:10,607 --> 00:03:12,859
But if you're willing
to face up to me, then…

76
00:03:12,942 --> 00:03:16,446
I am facing you,
but I'm not leaning either way right now.

77
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:20,575
There's a part of me
that's afraid of falling in love.

78
00:03:20,658 --> 00:03:23,828
That feeling of becoming total strangers
after breaking up.

79
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:26,623
When I think about that, it really hurts.

80
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:28,249
Then don't break up.

81
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,376
Well, yeah, that's right.

82
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,795
There's no point
in thinking about breaking up.

83
00:03:33,463 --> 00:03:35,298
Like, I'm thinking about marriage.

84
00:03:35,381 --> 00:03:38,635
If you're thinking about the future,
you should definitely choose me.

85
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:41,179
I can make you happier than he can.

86
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:57,362
I don't know anymore.
You don't know either, do you?

87
00:03:57,445 --> 00:03:58,279
I know.

88
00:03:58,363 --> 00:03:59,614
- You do?
- I know.

89
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:02,909
I mean, instead of choosing
between me and Taisei here,

90
00:04:02,992 --> 00:04:05,411
you should be comparing me
with all the guys across the country.

91
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:07,789
I'm willing to take on
anyone in that pool,

92
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:09,999
and I'm confident I can beat them.

93
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,626
So like, you don't have to be so confused.

94
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:13,711
- Leave it to me.
- But you're trying to confuse me.

95
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:14,754
That's right.

96
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:17,966
I don't know how I feel,
and that's exactly why, you know--

97
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:21,094
So, the goal for today is…
letting me hug you.

98
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:25,056
- You're too much.
- Hey, stand up for a sec.

99
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:27,016
- Oh, please.
- I wanna see how tall you are.

100
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:30,311
Just stand up for a sec.
I'm curious about the ceiling in here.

101
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:33,231
NAGANO

102
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:35,775
- I see what he did! It's the same trick!
- Oh, geez.

103
00:04:35,858 --> 00:04:38,778
When Ari goes to the sauna,
he ends up hugging the girl.

104
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:41,614
- He does this with everyone.
- Seems like it.

105
00:04:44,742 --> 00:04:46,828
- You're crushing me!
- How's that for ya?

106
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:54,752
- Mm.
- Sauna magic?

107
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,679
Wassup!

108
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:06,639
- Wassup?
- There she is.

109
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:08,891
- Sup, sup, sup!
- She's super hyped.

110
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:11,019
Pow, pow, pow! You know what it is.

111
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:14,022
Okay, so based on that vibe,
it must be a match with Ari?

112
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:16,232
Congrats.

113
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,276
- It felt way too good.
- Yeah.

114
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:19,902
That I was like…

115
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,029
…"I'm happy!"

116
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:24,866
- Like, the atmosphere…
- Yeah?

