HA-CHAN

138
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:22,799
EX-NO.1 HOST
CHASING TRUE LOVE

139
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:23,841
KAZU-KUN

140
00:06:56,707 --> 00:06:58,626
- Hey, hi.
- Morning.

141
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:04,298
I LOVE YOU

142
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:07,260
<i>You're halfway through</i>
<i>your time at this school.</i>

143
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:10,096
<i>To help everyone get closer,</i>

144
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:12,932
<i>alcohol is allowed today.</i>

145
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:14,851
- Thank you!
- That's great!

146
00:07:14,934 --> 00:07:16,561
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

147
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:19,439
- I humbly accept.
- Let's do it! Let's toast first.

148
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:22,108
- Okay, let's toast.
- Cheers!

149
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,365
- What are you making?
- Infinite bell peppers.

150
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:31,284
What's "infinite bell peppers"?

151
00:07:31,367 --> 00:07:32,910
Bell peppers you can eat endlessly.

152
00:07:32,994 --> 00:07:34,912
- I'll help. Let's make it together.
- I'll get started.

153
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:39,584
Teach me
how to make infinite bell peppers.

154
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:41,961
I don't really know. I'm just saying it.

155
00:07:42,044 --> 00:07:44,964
<i>Kazu-kun doesn't seem very good</i>
<i>at being aggressive.</i>

156
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,924
- <i>Right.</i>
- <i>He hasn't had to be.</i>

157
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:49,719
- Are we done bringing everything over?
- I think so.

158
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:50,928
- Let's go smoke.
- Okay.

159
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:55,600
<i>I wish she'd ask me to do something.</i>

160
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:57,268
<i>It's pretty much always Leo.</i>

161
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:03,483
I mean, I think I'm a pretty good catch.
I've got looks and money.

162
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:05,276
And I'm kind too.

163
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:08,905
But I'm really not the type
to initiate and be so aggressive.

164
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:12,825
Maybe this is the price for relying
on my looks and alcohol for so long.

165
00:08:16,996 --> 00:08:19,624
My weapons are useless.

166
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:21,667
So he has a weakness.

167
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:24,378
- It's impressive he's that self-aware.
- It is impressive.

168
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:25,922
It's kind of admirable.

169
00:08:26,964 --> 00:08:28,424
- Yoo-hoo.
- Hey there.

170
00:08:29,008 --> 00:08:30,510
- Isn't it cold?
- It's cold.

171
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:31,844
Come here.

172
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,096
- It's cold. Put this on.
- What?

173
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:35,181
RURU (26)
MODEL

174
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:36,140
LEO (25)
BAR OWNER

175
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:39,060
- Thanks.
- Yep.

176
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:43,064
Right now, all we're experiencing
is what happens in this environment.

177
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:43,981
Yeah.

178
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,776
But once we're released
back into our real lives,

179
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:48,653
we'll be long-distance, right?

180
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:49,779
Yeah.

181
00:08:49,862 --> 00:08:52,114
So I was thinking,
maybe we're being like this

182
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,991
only because of the environment

183
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:55,243
- we're in now.
- Yeah. I get that.

184
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,495
- So let's say we graduate.
- Yeah.

185
00:08:57,578 --> 00:09:00,164
- Say I end up with you, and we graduate.
- Mmm.

186
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:02,625
And we go back to the real world.

187
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:06,254
Like, I ask myself, "Do I have
the resolve not to cheat on Leo?"

188
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:07,171
Mmm.

189
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:10,091
I really think cheating
is like some sort of sickness.

190
00:09:10,174 --> 00:09:11,676
It's not a sickness.

191
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,928
- No. No.
- It can happen to anyone. For sure.

192
00:09:15,596 --> 00:09:18,015
I don't know if that's something
I'll ever fix about myself.

193
00:09:19,475 --> 00:09:20,893
What a confession!

194
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:28,901
I suppose if it ever does get fixed,
I'll be like "Wow, this is really love."

195
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:29,944
Mmm.

196
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:34,240
I know I won't chance it
when we're back in the world.

197
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:39,662
But as you know,
I have a history of cheating.

198
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:44,125
How can you trust me?
I wouldn't trust me. Never.

199
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:47,128
Because I already know
it's a sickness that can't be fixed.

200
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:50,339
- If anything, I'm glad you told me now.
- Mmm.

201
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:51,882
- But, but…
- Mmm?

202
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:54,468
It doesn't matter.

203
00:09:58,014 --> 00:09:59,974
Don't worry. I'll straighten you out.

204
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:03,352
What, you think I won't?

205
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,396
- Straighten me out?
- I guarantee I will.

206
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:10,401
He told me he'd fix my cheating habit.

207
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:15,531
Like, yeah, no one's said that before.

208
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:19,785
Seriously, the things he says to me
are just so incredibly sincere.

209
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:22,413
Yeah, I'm really touched.

210
00:10:23,247 --> 00:10:25,082
I mean, the things Leo says are just…

211
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,293
If we really do date…

212
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:30,630
I don't know how often it'll be,

213
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,591
but I kind of know he'll come see me.

214
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,968
I feel like he'd make me feel secure.

215
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:40,765
But my whole approach
to love is pretty distorted.

216
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:43,517
I don't know if I can be this open
when I face him.

217
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:47,855
I'm starting to feel scared
that I might hurt him.

218
00:10:47,938 --> 00:10:49,440
Mmm.

219
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:52,818
I really wish I hadn't had
such a distorted mindset

220
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:54,445
in my past relationships.

221
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:57,073
I feel like,
if I'd been more genuine then,

222
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:59,533
I could've gone for Leo
without holding back.

223
00:11:00,242 --> 00:11:02,953
But I've been way too distorted
when it comes to love.

224
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:11,504
You're taking forever over here.

225
00:11:11,587 --> 00:11:12,797
What?

226
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,090
You're talking too long.

227
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:15,758
- Are we?
- You brought tequila?

228
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:16,801
Let's do this.

229
00:11:16,884 --> 00:11:18,969
- What about our glasses?
- "Let's do this"? Right?

230
00:11:19,053 --> 00:11:20,221
Just been you the whole time?

231
00:11:20,304 --> 00:11:22,223
Yeah, we were just having
a deep conversation.

232
00:11:22,306 --> 00:11:25,226
- And you just ruined it with the tequila.
- Mmm.

233
00:11:25,309 --> 00:11:26,560
Thanks.

234
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:28,020
- See ya.
- Yeah.

235
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:30,398
Talk later.

236
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:32,525
<i>He's nice enough to step aside.</i>

237
00:11:32,608 --> 00:11:33,567
All right.

238
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:36,320
I think I'm done drinking for tonight.

239
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:38,906
- <i>He's a real man.</i>
- <i>Nice.</i>

240
00:11:38,989 --> 00:11:39,990
MAX MANLINESS

241
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:43,202
- So you just came to talk?
- That's right.

242
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:47,164
I think a transfer student
should definitely shake things up.

243
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:48,791
No, no, no, it's hard, though.

244
00:11:48,874 --> 00:11:51,502
I know it's hard.
It would be hard for me too.

245
00:11:51,585 --> 00:11:53,838
I mean, a lot of us already know
who we're into.

246
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:55,840
I mean, it's already bad.

247
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:57,758
- What is?
- Well, um…

248
00:11:58,426 --> 00:12:00,386
- The other day, on Valentine's Day…
- Yeah?

249
00:12:00,469 --> 00:12:02,096
…you told me to stay next to you.

250
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:04,682
- Mmm.
- But doesn't that go both ways?

251
00:12:06,016 --> 00:12:09,854
I mean, if there's a girl
you even slightly want to talk to,

252
00:12:09,937 --> 00:12:10,980
you can be more aggressive.

253
00:12:11,981 --> 00:12:14,150
- I can't.
- Yes, you can.

254
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:15,609
I love my friends.

255
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:16,944
Okay.

256
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:20,239
Once I become friends with someone,
I can't help but back him up.

257
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:21,157
Yeah.

258
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,409
If it's between a girl and a guy,
I'd choose the guy.

259
00:12:23,492 --> 00:12:25,619
- Yeah, right. I get that too.
- Yeah. That's why…

260
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:29,331
Right, that's why I said I didn't want
to make friends with them.

261
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:30,332
- I get that.
- Yeah.

262
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:32,293
- So, that hasn't really changed.
- Right.

263
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:34,044
What happens is,

264
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:37,131
I talk to them every day,
more than I do with the girls.

265
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:38,632
So I end up getting close to them.

266
00:12:38,716 --> 00:12:39,967
- Yeah, you do.
- Yeah.

267
00:12:40,050 --> 00:12:42,887
Like, if you were sitting next to Leo,
I couldn't just come in.

268
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:46,432
I see. Yeah, you can't do that
if you care about your friends.

269
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:47,892
He's a good guy.

270
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:49,435
He's actually a good guy.

271
00:12:49,518 --> 00:12:51,479
He must've really pushed himself
at the beginning.

272
00:12:51,562 --> 00:12:53,522
- He even got in a fight.
- Yeah.

273
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:58,235
Honestly, I cannot tell
how serious you are about me,

274
00:12:58,319 --> 00:13:00,988
or if and how much
you like the other girls.

275
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:04,533
Shouldn't you try
to make me trust in you more?

276
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:07,953
Why are you being so passive in all this?

277
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:10,331
I'm not being passive,
I'm trying to look inside.

278
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:11,540
- Yeah.
- Really.

279
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:15,085
Listen, my exes were ugly as hell.

280
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:16,670
All of them.

281
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:18,923
Really, they were all so ugly,
everyone would agree.

282
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:21,675
- I feel bad for Leo.
- What? No, I didn't mean Leo.

283
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:22,968
- He's not my ex.
- No, no.

284
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:25,888
I'm just trying to say that
I'm the type who looks at what's inside.

285
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:28,182
- Oh, yeah.
- I mean, you're such a good-looking guy.

286
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:31,644
Anyone would agree
that you're a very good-looking guy.

287
00:13:32,686 --> 00:13:34,855
I mean, we can all control
how we look on the outside.

288
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:36,148
I've had work done.

289
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:38,984
Anyone can change their looks.
Personality is what counts.

290
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:41,737
Man, Ruru is so cool.

291
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:45,282
Damn, these women
are gonna drive me crazy.

292
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:47,117
Come on, you're a transfer student.

293
00:13:47,201 --> 00:13:49,870
- Try harder and show me how you feel!
- No, no, no.

294
00:13:50,454 --> 00:13:52,665
Everyone's here to find love.
Guys and girls.

295
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:56,961
So when you say,
"You're the one who's not making a move,"

296
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:58,504
it kind of gets on my nerves.

297
00:13:58,587 --> 00:14:01,423
Oh, but I'm leaning toward Leo right now.

298
00:14:02,132 --> 00:14:03,259
That's what I'm telling you.

299
00:14:03,342 --> 00:14:06,303
So if you have feelings for me,
it's for you to make a move on me.

300
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:07,888
- Don't you think?
- Okay, wait.

301
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:09,348
- Hold on. I get that.
- Yeah.

302
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:13,477
<i>I never met a host I could trust.</i>

303
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:16,856
I tend to go in
with a "you can't fool me" attitude.

304
00:14:17,648 --> 00:14:19,608
I care about personality,
and I want someone

305
00:14:19,692 --> 00:14:22,194
who comes at me straight
with their feelings.

306
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:25,948
I told Kazuma that he's good-looking,
but I'll judge him by his personality.

307
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:29,326
That was just some flexing.

308
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:30,494
On my part, that is.

309
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:32,538
With my actions and stuff.

310
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:37,376
Today kind of made me
make up my mind. Yeah.

311
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:38,294
I feel like…

312
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:42,298
like what I need is to be more aggressive.

313
00:14:43,632 --> 00:14:45,718
It's all really offense from here.

314
00:14:47,845 --> 00:14:50,472
If you won't sing, I'll make you sing…

315
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:52,683
Ruru bird.

316
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:54,435
<i>What?</i>

317
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:56,812
<i>He's laughing out loud to himself.</i>

318
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:59,273
You could tell he wasn't confident
from the "singing" line alone.

319
00:14:59,356 --> 00:15:01,358
- For sure.
- Like, "What do I do?"

320
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:03,569
He was trying
to be careful with his words,

321
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:04,653
and the tension was rising.

322
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:06,030
That happens a lot to me as well.

323
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:07,239
Oh, me too.

324
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:09,658
I start to go, "Hahaha,"
and no one's laughing.

325
00:15:11,785 --> 00:15:13,495
Is this lemon sour?

326
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:15,456
Yeah, sour lemon.
I'm having iichiko<i>.</i>

327
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:16,707
- Okay.
- Yeah.

328
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:19,251
- So, what about you, Marina?
- What do you mean?

329
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:22,171
Seriously, I have no idea what's going on
with your love life around here.

330
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:24,048
Well, I have nothing.

331
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:26,926
Don't you have anyone
you're interested in?

332
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:28,510
Or anyone you think is nice?

333
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:30,846
I mean, everyone seems to be
in full-on happy mode,

334
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,015
and I feel like
I'm the only one who came here

335
00:15:33,098 --> 00:15:35,392
to take this seriously or something.

336
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,436
- But that's fine, right? I mean…
- Yeah.

337
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:39,313
- Well…
- Yeah?

338
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:41,357
It's okay if you're into someone taken.

339
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:43,567
- The other guys are. Yeah.
- Well, yeah, that's true.

340
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,611
So…

341
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:47,279
Has anyone's face caught your eye?

342
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:49,365
- Their face?
- Their face, the way they talk and stuff?

343
00:15:49,448 --> 00:15:50,991
Well, you look exactly like my ex.

344
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:53,452
Oh, wow. Oh, wow.

345
00:15:53,535 --> 00:15:55,454
- Yeah, there are lots of guys,
- Yeah.

346
00:15:55,537 --> 00:15:57,998
But the only one
who looks like my ex here is you.

347
00:15:58,082 --> 00:16:00,376
- Oh, man.
- Don't be so awkward about it.

348
00:16:00,459 --> 00:16:02,503
I can't say anything, 'cause I'm already…

349
00:16:02,586 --> 00:16:04,171
- I only have eyes for Asuka.
- Yeah, I know.

350
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:06,256
I'm not an option for you.
Sorry about that.

351
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,341
I know.

352
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:09,134
BUDDHA LEAN

353
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:11,053
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

354
00:16:12,304 --> 00:16:14,223
I have something
I wanted to tell you today.

355
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:15,265
What is it?

356
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:18,394
I thought about it today,
and I still like you, Asuka.

357
00:16:18,477 --> 00:16:19,395
I think you're pretty.

358
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:21,021
ASSUN (30)
ENTREPRENEUR/HOSTESS

359
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,731
That's all.

360
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:23,649
MA-KUN (28)
MMA FIGHTER

361
00:16:23,732 --> 00:16:25,109
You're adorable.

362
00:16:27,945 --> 00:16:28,988
That's all.

363
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,283
I was debating
with myself a bit yesterday.

364
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:37,204
Like, "What would happen to us
after our time here is over?"

365
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:38,122
Mmm.

366
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:40,249
Everyone's starting to worry about that.

367
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:41,917
It's like being under a spell.

368
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:45,337
Yeah, I definitely think that's how it is.
It's this environment.

369
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:48,424
I'm not planning
on leaving Gunma right away.

370
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,009
- Yeah.
- I don't think I can.

371
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:54,555
That said, if I'm going to think
about being with you,

372
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:58,475
there are things I'll have to change
somewhere along the line.

373
00:17:02,604 --> 00:17:03,856
- <i>Oh?</i>
- <i>Oh!</i>

374
00:17:03,939 --> 00:17:05,649
- Won't I?
- <i>My heart skipped a beat.</i>

375
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:06,692
Yeah, you're right.

376
00:17:06,775 --> 00:17:08,193
- <i>Hey!</i>
- Not so fast.

377
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:09,486
We're saving ourselves.

378
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:17,327
- Listen.
- Hmm.

379
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:18,704
LOVEY-DOVEY

380
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:20,539
<i>I mean, I know what you're like.</i>

381
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:23,834
<i>That's why I was so worried yesterday.</i>

382
00:17:24,501 --> 00:17:27,463
- Deep down, I'm a serious person.
- I know.

383
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:28,797
Yeah, I'm a straight shooter.

384
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:31,967
Exactly, it's your straight nature
that's making me debate with myself!

385
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:32,885
Understood.

386
00:17:34,386 --> 00:17:35,471
No, I got it.

387
00:17:35,554 --> 00:17:36,972
- I'm sorry.
- Yeah.

388
00:17:40,851 --> 00:17:42,311
Man, that hurt.

389
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:44,480
What did?

390
00:17:45,522 --> 00:17:46,815
- The kiss?
- Of course.

391
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:47,733
Kiss.

392
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:51,820
Ah.

393
00:17:53,989 --> 00:17:56,408
I'm serious.
I'm really serious about you, Asuka.

394
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:58,243
No, I mean it.

395
00:18:01,538 --> 00:18:02,372
- Bo.
- Hmm?

396
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:04,958
It's a good day. Another good day today.

397
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:06,168
How was it?

398
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:08,670
I asked for a kiss, and she kissed me.

399
00:18:08,754 --> 00:18:11,465
<i>He tells them everything.</i>

400
00:18:11,548 --> 00:18:14,593
Wait, so tell us more.
Was it the French kind?

401
00:18:15,135 --> 00:18:17,137
- Yeah, it was French.
- You know what's next.

402
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:19,556
The D, man, the D.

403
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,725
The D, man. She wants the D.

404
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:24,186
- We're experienced men here.
- Oh, my God.

405
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:26,355
And the most advanced thing
that's happened is a kiss.

406
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:27,773
- I mean, isn't that crazy?
- Yeah.

407
00:18:27,856 --> 00:18:30,025
And it's French too. Come on!

408
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:31,819
- No doubt.
- Hey, I gotta ask you.

409
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:34,404
- Were your eyes open or closed?
- Closed, okay.

410
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:37,908
- So lame. You gotta go like this.
- So lame.

411
00:18:37,991 --> 00:18:39,910
- <i>So adorable!</i>
- <i>They're so adorable.</i>

412
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:45,249
- That's wassup.
- Don't say that.

413
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:47,709
- That's wassup.
- That's wassup.

414
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:51,463
It's like I'm under the magic
of <i>Badly In Love. </i>For real.

415
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:54,049
- The TV magic?
- Yeah, I'm under the TV magic.

416
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:57,427
I have a certain line I don't cross.

417
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:00,055
I was kinda like, "Kissing is a little…"

418
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,807
- <i>That's a surprise.</i>
- <i>Really?</i>

419
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:05,352
Apparently, I was drunk
and saying stuff like, "Let's kiss,"

420
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:06,645
but I'm not so sure.

421
00:19:07,396 --> 00:19:08,272
I don't remember it.

422
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:09,773
- <i>Oh, my.</i>
- <i>There it is.</i>

423
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:14,945
<i>Ichiro, the baseball player,</i>
<i>once said something I take to heart.</i>

424
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:18,448
<i>It's that people's judgment</i>
<i>tends to get worse at night.</i>

425
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:22,911
Wait, Ichiro as in the Ichiro?

426
00:19:22,995 --> 00:19:25,164
Yes, apparently
they're from the same hometown.

427
00:19:25,747 --> 00:19:28,125
I'm still not really sure what to do.

428
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:33,922
<i>I haven't fallen for him yet.</i>
<i>It takes time for me too.</i>

429
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:35,299
<i>What?</i>

430
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:40,345
- Hey, wait.
- What?

431
00:19:40,929 --> 00:19:42,556
- Plot twist.
- Huh?

432
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:44,850
So that wasn't the "I like you" kiss?

433
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:47,227
<i>- But she clearly went for it.</i>
- <i>Yeah.</i>

434
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:48,187
<i>She tried it.</i>

435
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,647
<i>He would never think</i>
<i>she wouldn't remember this.</i>

436
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:54,401
If they had listened to Mr. Ichiro
and taken their time,

437
00:19:54,484 --> 00:19:56,528
if they kissed in the morning,
it's a different story.

438
00:19:56,612 --> 00:19:57,529
Oh, right.

439
00:19:57,613 --> 00:20:01,450
Mr. Ichiro never said anything
about kissing in the morning, okay?

440
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:03,327
He was talking
about mental attitude or something.

441
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:08,457
So now, we also have a love triangle
forming between Ruru, Leo, and Kazu-kun.

442
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:10,834
Ruru's great. She's so refreshing.

443
00:20:10,918 --> 00:20:14,296
You could say she's leaving
all the options open on the table

444
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:15,839
- for Leo and Kazu-kun.
- Yeah.

445
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:19,593
She's basically saying,
"Here. Have all the information."

446
00:20:19,676 --> 00:20:22,054
"So, if you want to do something,
go ahead."

447
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:23,847
True, she's being fair and transparent.

448
00:20:23,931 --> 00:20:26,808
But isn't saying you'll cheat
pretty extreme by itself?

449
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:28,352
It's super extreme.

450
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:31,021
It really shows you how much resolve
she's coming here with.

451
00:20:31,104 --> 00:20:32,856
- Yeah. I tell people everything.
- You do?

452
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:35,192
When I like someone,
I show all my cards right away.

453
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:36,443
Really?

454
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:38,820
So I really understand how Ruru feels.

455
00:20:38,904 --> 00:20:42,991
But if you tell them that,
you risk not being chosen in the end,

456
00:20:44,117 --> 00:20:46,536
and there's that chance
that you'll end up lonely

457
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:48,455
for the rest of your life.

458
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:49,957
Then why does she tell them?

459
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:52,209
Because he wants to be loved
for who she is.

460
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:53,418
Ah, I see.

461
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:55,087
I think that's the kind of bond

462
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:57,798
- she's craving deeply in a relationship.
- I see.

463
00:20:57,881 --> 00:21:01,551
So Kazu-kun, Leo, and Ruru
are all starting to look like nice people.

464
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:03,136
- They're all nice.
- For sure.

465
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,054
They really are.

466
00:21:04,137 --> 00:21:04,972
It's true.

467
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:07,182
Everyone in this love triangle is so nice.

468
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:09,017
- It's hard to pick sides.
- Tough choice.

469
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:12,271
They're so different from Hikaru's group.
Hikaru's group and Ruru's group.

470
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:13,689
- That's a mess.
- That's another story.

471
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:15,190
They're a total mess.

472
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,275
- Yeah.
- All of them.

473
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:18,777
Like, I want them to be happy,
but what can you do?

474
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:20,153
- Yeah, right?
- Yeah.

475
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:21,571
They should be a throuple.

476
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:23,448
- Right, that would be new.
- Right.

477
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:25,575
- And they can cheat all they want.
- A new shape of love.

478
00:21:26,159 --> 00:21:27,744
- It'll be new.
- She can cheat.

479
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:37,337
<i>You have free time this afternoon.</i>

480
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:39,006
<i>Is this prison?</i>

481
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:41,133
- <i>It's not prison.</i>
- <i>It is not prison.</i>

482
00:21:41,717 --> 00:21:45,137
<i>If there is someone</i>
<i>you don't know very well yet,</i>

483
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:49,808
<i>or a person you're interested in,</i>
<i>get to know them better.</i>

484
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:52,894
LOVE DINER

485
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:53,812
So…

486
00:21:53,895 --> 00:21:56,023
- I was planning on telling you this today.
- Yeah?

487
00:21:56,106 --> 00:22:00,319
I've been talking to mostly Ari so far,
but I figured he'd choose Hikaru.

488
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:02,404
But now I'm going back to the guy
I liked at the start.

489
00:22:02,487 --> 00:22:03,780
- Yeah, yeah.
- To Tai-chan.

490
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,949
I'm gonna try talking to him some more.

491
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:08,118
- Oh, I see. Yeah, that's a good idea.
- Yeah, so…

492
00:22:08,201 --> 00:22:11,330
I'm not sure if I actually like him,
but I think I'll try being

493
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:14,416
- a little more proactive in my own way.
- Oh, that's great to hear, Marina.

494
00:22:14,499 --> 00:22:15,751
- Wait.
- Watch the knife.

495
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:17,586
- That's so great.
- Thanks.

496
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:18,628
<i>Ohh!</i>

497
00:22:18,712 --> 00:22:20,922
<i>Oh, it's great that she's moving on.</i>

498
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:22,257
- <i>Good luck.</i>
- <i>Yeah.</i>

499
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:23,175
<i>Really.</i>

500
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:26,803
Oh. Hey.

501
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:28,263
You look shady. Yoo-hoo.

502
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:31,058
- How are you?
- I wonder how it's going.

503
00:22:31,141 --> 00:22:33,060
- How it's going?
- How's it going for you?

504
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:35,687
- How are you? With Ari.
- You wanna talk about me?

505
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:37,272
Well, why not?

506
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,441
No, no, no. I don't know about him.

507
00:22:39,524 --> 00:22:41,735
- Yeah.
- He's still going over to talk to Hikaru.

508
00:22:41,818 --> 00:22:42,652
Yeah.

509
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:44,821
Right, you like her. You know.

510
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:47,866
Hmm…

511
00:22:47,949 --> 00:22:49,868
- You're stressing over it too, huh?
- Well, of course.

512
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:51,661
I guess it's time to show my skills.

513
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:54,748
That's funny.

514
00:22:55,957 --> 00:22:58,043
We haven't talked in this classroom
since that night.

515
00:22:59,127 --> 00:23:01,505
So if this is the kind of guy you are,
none of us need you, okay?

516
00:23:01,588 --> 00:23:02,923
<i>There it is.</i>

517
00:23:03,006 --> 00:23:05,133
- I honestly think you're a piece of trash.
- Mmm.

518
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:06,259
<i>Trash.</i>

519
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:09,930
If you don't change,
if you can't act like a man,

520
00:23:10,013 --> 00:23:11,681
then no one
is going to love you, Tai-chan.

521
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:12,599
Mmm-hmm.

522
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:15,727
That was scary.

523
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:19,022
I thought one of them was gonna stab me.

524
00:23:20,315 --> 00:23:21,358
He's so gentle.

525
00:23:21,441 --> 00:23:22,776
Tai-chan.

526
00:23:23,276 --> 00:23:25,362
- But it went by so fast.
- Yeah.

527
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:28,031
Let's end this without any regrets.

528
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:29,449
- Yeah, you're right.
- Yeah.

529
00:23:32,536 --> 00:23:34,162
- Too soon?
- No.

530
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:36,206
<i>Oh, it's Ha-chan.</i>

531
00:23:36,289 --> 00:23:38,625
- Well, good luck.
- You too.

532
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:41,753
Hey.

533
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:45,715
- Was it too soon?
- No, not at all.

534
00:23:46,341 --> 00:23:48,135
But it looks like you're really torn.

535
00:23:48,718 --> 00:23:49,553
- Me?
- Yeah.

536
00:23:49,636 --> 00:23:50,887
Of course I would be torn.

537
00:23:50,971 --> 00:23:53,557
I can really tell.
Well, Hikaru seems really torn too.

538
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,142
- Hikaru?
- Yeah.

539
00:23:56,476 --> 00:23:57,686
I see.

540
00:23:57,769 --> 00:24:01,857
Anyway, I've been telling her about you
without hiding or anything.

541
00:24:02,941 --> 00:24:04,067
Hmm?

542
00:24:04,151 --> 00:24:06,945
I've told her how I'm feeling,
that I'm interested in you.

543
00:24:07,654 --> 00:24:08,488
Oh, really?

544
00:24:08,572 --> 00:24:12,701
But I don't want that to get in the way,
to keep Hikaru from going for you.

545
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:15,036
- Oh, okay.
- It's for you to decide.

546
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:18,665
It's not up to me.
You think it is? Really?

547
00:24:18,748 --> 00:24:20,750
I had to muster up some courage
to say this.

548
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:23,795
- Really? You had to psyche up?
- Yeah. Yeah, I did.

549
00:24:24,421 --> 00:24:26,590
I've never made the first move in my life.

550
00:24:26,673 --> 00:24:28,508
- Oh, really?
- No, never.

551
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:32,220
- Should I raid their conversation?
- Go ahead.

552
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:36,433
- I'm going out.
- See ya.

553
00:24:38,477 --> 00:24:39,853
<i>Where's she going?</i>

554
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,106
Ta-da!

555
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:44,399
Oh!

556
00:24:44,483 --> 00:24:45,901
My first raid!

557
00:24:45,984 --> 00:24:47,611
- <i>What?</i>
- Hey, can I talk to her?

558
00:24:47,694 --> 00:24:48,987
- Just the two of us?
- Sure.

559
00:24:49,070 --> 00:24:50,197
- Is that okay?
- Yeah.

560
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,823
Okay. You wanna sit here?

561
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:53,742
- Yeah, thanks.
- Okay, then.

562
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:57,120
- I wanted to have a chat with you.
- Okay.

563
00:24:57,204 --> 00:25:01,666
Well, I thought about it a lot,
but I'm here to find love too, so…

564
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:02,584
Yeah.

565
00:25:02,667 --> 00:25:04,711
I've been spending
most of my time with Leo.

566
00:25:04,794 --> 00:25:08,507
Leo's been so focused on me,
so I felt I should do the same.

567
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:10,967
- Yeah.
- But our time here's limited.

568
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:12,928
- That's right.
- So I thought there might be

569
00:25:13,011 --> 00:25:15,096
- someone here I could fall for.
- Yeah.

570
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,974
But maybe I just haven't had
the chance to talk to him yet.

571
00:25:18,558 --> 00:25:19,726
Oh.

572
00:25:19,809 --> 00:25:22,062
Yeah, and for me, that person was you.

573
00:25:22,145 --> 00:25:23,980
We both live in Tokyo too.

574
00:25:24,064 --> 00:25:27,234
- Oh. Seriously?
- Yeah. Yeah, so I came to talk to you now.

575
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:29,653
Thank you, thank you.

576
00:25:29,736 --> 00:25:31,821
- I'm so happy. Honestly, thank you.
- Yeah.

577
00:25:32,405 --> 00:25:34,241
I mean,
I didn't think I'd get to talk to you.

578
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:35,158
Right.

579
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:37,494
I mean, I was sure you and Leo,

580
00:25:37,994 --> 00:25:41,248
you know, how you are,
you both seem so into each other.

581
00:25:41,331 --> 00:25:44,125
Well, I think if I had
stronger feelings for Leo,

582
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:45,961
- I'd be more focused on him.
- Yeah.

583
00:25:46,044 --> 00:25:48,505
And I probably wouldn't be talking
to anyone else.

584
00:25:48,588 --> 00:25:50,507
- Yeah.
- But the thing with Leo…

585
00:25:50,590 --> 00:25:53,760
the thing about dating him
in real life is the distance.

586
00:25:54,261 --> 00:25:57,264
- Oh, since he's in Kyoto.
- He's in Kyoto, and I'm in Tokyo.

587
00:25:57,347 --> 00:25:59,182
It'll be long-distance.

588
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:01,518
When we go back to reality,
there will be temptations,

589
00:26:01,601 --> 00:26:02,811
and I can't say what will happen.

590
00:26:02,894 --> 00:26:04,688
It's not like we live close enough

591
00:26:04,771 --> 00:26:07,065
to just stay over at each other's places.

592
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,942
- That's true.
- Since we live in different cities.

593
00:26:09,025 --> 00:26:11,027
So that's what's been holding me back
this whole time.

594
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:12,445
- Ah, so it's the distance?
- With Leo.

595
00:26:12,529 --> 00:26:13,989
Yeah, the distance.

596
00:26:14,072 --> 00:26:16,783
- I really look at people's personalities.
- Mmm.

597
00:26:16,866 --> 00:26:20,287
Like how they act around others,
what kind of personality they have.

598
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:22,998
Isn't everything about me a negative?

599
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:25,292
- You don't think?
- But you've changed.

600
00:26:25,375 --> 00:26:26,585
- You think so?
- You've changed.

601
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:28,628
If you hadn't, I wouldn't have come here.

602
00:26:30,338 --> 00:26:33,675
I mean, I like guys who bring out
my maternal instincts.

603
00:26:33,758 --> 00:26:34,676
Hmm.

604
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:37,804
When a strong man shows
a bit of his vulnerable side,

605
00:26:37,887 --> 00:26:40,098
it brings out those maternal instincts,

606
00:26:40,181 --> 00:26:43,518
and I feel like I need to help him,
or do something for him.

607
00:26:43,602 --> 00:26:44,936
- I think that's love.
- Mmm.

608
00:26:45,020 --> 00:26:47,522
Like, "Oh, Tai-chan
has this cute side to him."

609
00:26:47,606 --> 00:26:48,440
Mmm.

610
00:26:48,523 --> 00:26:51,901
I thought you were really adorable.
I don't feel that way about Leo.

611
00:26:51,985 --> 00:26:53,612
- He's always like a real man.
- That's true.

612
00:26:53,695 --> 00:26:56,573
He's always been straight with me.
He doesn't really lean on me,

613
00:26:56,656 --> 00:26:59,451
- so that instinct doesn't come out.
- Yeah, yeah. Yeah.

614
00:26:59,534 --> 00:27:02,287
But you do bring it out,
so I wanted to chat with you a bit.

615
00:27:02,370 --> 00:27:03,538
Oh, really?

616
00:27:04,247 --> 00:27:05,790
- Thanks.
- So talk to me.

617
00:27:05,874 --> 00:27:07,709
- Okay.
- We haven't had a chance to get close

618
00:27:07,792 --> 00:27:09,502
like Ma-kun and Assun are.

619
00:27:09,586 --> 00:27:11,713
- Okay.
- So don't be shy and just talk to me.

620
00:27:11,796 --> 00:27:13,256
- Okay.
- I'll talk to you too.

621
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,884
- My heart's still pounding.
- Why is it pounding?

622
00:27:15,967 --> 00:27:18,970
- It's crazy. My heart's pounding.
- That's cute.

623
00:27:20,472 --> 00:27:22,015
Things are starting to move.

624
00:27:24,100 --> 00:27:25,644
It's finally happening.

625
00:27:27,187 --> 00:27:29,105
I didn't think this could ever happen.

626
00:27:29,606 --> 00:27:31,983
Her outfit today was insane.

627
00:27:32,067 --> 00:27:33,401
<i>Yeah, I was shocked.</i>

628
00:27:34,402 --> 00:27:35,528
<i>It made my heart race.</i>

629
00:27:36,780 --> 00:27:39,574
- I feel like I'm starting to fall for her.
- <i>Oh?</i>

630
00:27:39,658 --> 00:27:40,992
I'm falling for Ruru.

631
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:43,578
Remind yourself of that night, Tai-chan.

632
00:27:43,662 --> 00:27:47,457
- She scolded you.
- If you date, that will be your life.

633
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:48,667
Hikaru.

634
00:27:49,876 --> 00:27:50,710
Ruru.

635
00:27:51,878 --> 00:27:53,254
I'm the youngest one here…

636
00:27:54,422 --> 00:27:56,633
and it's time for me
to snatch them all up.

637
00:27:58,093 --> 00:28:00,470
I guess my time has finally come.

638
00:28:02,055 --> 00:28:04,724
Wait a second, who was Tai-chan into
at the beginning?

639
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:05,934
I think it was Ruru.

640
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:07,394
- It was Ruru?
- It was Ruru.

641
00:28:07,477 --> 00:28:10,730
Tai-chan started liking Hikaru
after the letter mix-up.

642
00:28:10,814 --> 00:28:12,023
- Right.
- Oh, right.

643
00:28:12,107 --> 00:28:13,525
- He started liking her.
- I see.

644
00:28:13,608 --> 00:28:17,904
So the first person Tai-chan went after
based on his own feelings

645
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:19,280
was Ruru.

646
00:28:20,115 --> 00:28:22,826
- That's why you're here, Sensei.
- I'd forgotten about that.

647
00:28:23,451 --> 00:28:26,413
- She's amazing.
- Sensei's memory is remarkable too.

648
00:28:26,496 --> 00:28:28,331
- Yeah, it's great.
- And her analysis.

649
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:30,083
So when Lady Ruru raided…

650
00:28:30,166 --> 00:28:31,209
Right.

651
00:28:31,292 --> 00:28:33,628
She came to him, he suddenly remembered.

652
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:35,422
He never thought he'd get a chance.

653
00:28:35,505 --> 00:28:37,298
And his crush came to see him herself.

654
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:40,093
Did you see that endorphin face he made
when she walked in?

655
00:28:40,176 --> 00:28:41,010
<i>Whoa.</i>

656
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:43,430
<i>So this is an endorphin face,</i>
<i>anatomically speaking.</i>

657
00:28:43,513 --> 00:28:44,514
<i>Yes.</i>

658
00:28:46,599 --> 00:28:47,892
MEN

659
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:50,729
Maririn might be a bit of a femme fatale.

660
00:28:50,812 --> 00:28:52,939
- Yeah.
- Yeah, I think she is.

661
00:28:53,022 --> 00:28:53,898
What?

662
00:28:53,982 --> 00:28:56,401
- What? Maririn?
- Wait, Maririn isn't…

663
00:28:56,484 --> 00:28:57,318
What?

664
00:28:58,653 --> 00:29:01,197
She was like,
"You're just like my abusive ex."

665
00:29:01,281 --> 00:29:05,243
"Your personality, your looks,
everything about you is exactly like him."

666
00:29:05,326 --> 00:29:07,245
- Oh, really?
- I was like, "Wait, what?"

667
00:29:08,037 --> 00:29:11,332
She only said it to me.
When we were alone.

668
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:14,127
She did say you're her type
and made a move on you.

669
00:29:14,210 --> 00:29:18,673
Well, I like guys with scary faces,
and you're the only one who's a bit scary.

670
00:29:19,507 --> 00:29:21,676
- I look the scariest?
- You kinda look scary.

671
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:23,219
I meant "scary" as a compliment.

672
00:29:23,303 --> 00:29:26,347
Oh, but everyone always says
that I've got a scary face.

673
00:29:26,848 --> 00:29:30,769
And she said
that Tai-chan's face is her type too.

674
00:29:31,269 --> 00:29:33,438
You caught my attention first,
so I wrote you the letter--

675
00:29:33,521 --> 00:29:34,939
Me? Not Leo?

676
00:29:35,023 --> 00:29:36,900
- Huh? No.
- Didn't you say it was Leo?

677
00:29:36,983 --> 00:29:38,610
- No, it was you.
- The guys were saying that.

678
00:29:38,693 --> 00:29:40,987
I gave you the letter and wrote
that I was interested, right?

679
00:29:41,070 --> 00:29:41,905
Oh.

680
00:29:42,489 --> 00:29:43,823
- At the beginning.
- She did say that.

681
00:29:43,907 --> 00:29:46,326
- That's right, she did, I almost forgot.
- Right.

682
00:29:46,409 --> 00:29:49,078
<i>Maririn was massaging Bo's shoulders</i>

683
00:29:49,162 --> 00:29:50,663
<i>and hugged him in the picture.</i>

684
00:29:51,164 --> 00:29:52,457
<i>I saw her do that too.</i>

685
00:29:53,666 --> 00:29:55,210
<i>She's going after everyone.</i>

686
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:59,047
<i>Oh, wow, what are you doing?</i>

687
00:30:00,340 --> 00:30:03,510
Just imagine how she talks
when she's with the girls,

688
00:30:03,593 --> 00:30:05,845
and how she talks
when she's alone with a guy.

689
00:30:05,929 --> 00:30:07,138
She's totally different.

690
00:30:10,433 --> 00:30:13,269
What's with the Maririn
character assassination all of a sudden?

691
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:14,521
She's being slandered.

692
00:30:14,604 --> 00:30:16,231
These guys don't get it at all.

693
00:30:17,524 --> 00:30:21,361
So, of all the guys,
who do you actually like the most, Marina?

694
00:30:21,945 --> 00:30:25,240
Well, if we're talking about looks,
then Tai-chan's my favorite.

695
00:30:25,323 --> 00:30:28,076
- Yeah, you said that.
- And I told Ari I think he's handsome.

696
00:30:28,159 --> 00:30:31,037
- Mmm.
- I told Leo he's handsome too.

697
00:30:31,120 --> 00:30:32,247
- And…
- Yeah.

698
00:30:32,330 --> 00:30:33,915
- Earlier, Ma-kun told me…
- Yeah.

699
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:37,919
He told me that you had said to him
that he was your type.

700
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:39,337
That's not what she said.

701
00:30:39,420 --> 00:30:40,755
She didn't say that.

702
00:30:40,839 --> 00:30:43,758
- Ma-kun is blowing it out of proportion.
- Yeah.

703
00:30:44,342 --> 00:30:45,260
Wait, no, no.

704
00:30:45,343 --> 00:30:48,721
What happened was,
I got asked who my type was.

705
00:30:48,805 --> 00:30:52,016
- Then I told him, "You look like my ex."
- Yeah.

706
00:30:52,100 --> 00:30:56,104
And he said, "But I like Assun."
I never meant it that way though.

707
00:30:56,187 --> 00:31:00,149
I'm a nightlife worker,
so I tend to build people up when I talk.

708
00:31:00,233 --> 00:31:01,901
- It's just a habit.
- Yeah.

709
00:31:01,985 --> 00:31:04,112
And I ended up talking to him
that way too.

710
00:31:04,195 --> 00:31:05,029
Mmm, mmm.

711
00:31:05,113 --> 00:31:07,824
So, I'm sorry if I gave
you and Ma-kun the wrong idea.

712
00:31:08,449 --> 00:31:09,325
But let me say…

713
00:31:10,994 --> 00:31:12,996
You all told me that we're friends,

714
00:31:13,079 --> 00:31:15,874
so I would never do anything
to betray you.

715
00:31:15,957 --> 00:31:18,751
- I'll tell you before I do anything.
- Mmm.

716
00:31:18,835 --> 00:31:22,338
But I think I definitely said it
the wrong way.

